  "reply_text": "*One merge-blocking finding.*\n\n*Critical — `src/guard.js:12`: View-only shares can edit unlocked documents.*\n`share.mask & WRITE === WRITE` parses as `share.mask & (WRITE === WRITE)`, so it checks the READ bit (`1`), not WRITE (`4`). I reproduced `canEdit({ mask: READ, locked: false })` returning `true`; a WRITE-only share is incorrectly denied.\n\n*Recommended fix:* Use `hasRight(share.mask, WRITE) && !share.locked`. Add regression tests denying edits for READ-only and READ|COMMENT shares, and allowing WRITE-only shares.\n\nAll 6 existing tests pass, but they miss these cases. No other findings in the full diff against `main`. No files changed.",
